PETSELFTEST1
# V6-02 fixed voice commands on the pet. "vcmd" steps inject the wire names
# the server's matcher would send (the board's real command path; the XiaoZhi
# MCP tool that carries them from the server is a later step). Counted from
# "mark begin" (see tools/selftest_report.py).
# Every command logs one PET_VOICE_CMD line with its result.
# expect min:name=PAGE_NEXT 2
# expect min:name=TELL_TIME 1
# expect min:name=TELL_BATTERY 2
# expect min:name=OPEN_READER 1
# expect min:name=SLEEP_REQUEST 1
# Next page at home, an unknown name, and a status answer over a book are
# refused or ignored; battery, reader and sleep requests are done.
# expect min:result=not_in_reader 1
# expect min:result=unknown 1
# expect min:result=busy 1
# expect min:result=done 3
# SLEEP_REQUEST runs the V2-09 flow and is cancelled by a key press while
# the sleeping picture is still coming up: nothing powers off.
# expect min:PET_SLEEP_REQUESTED 1
# expect min:PET_SLEEP_CANCELLED 1
# expect none:PET_SLEEP_POWEROFF 0
# expect none:PET_SELFTEST_ABORT 0
# expect selftest_done 1
# Quiet prompts while testing (RAM only, this boot).
volume 15
waitidle 60000
pet
wait 6000
# Normalize restored pet state to "home, neutral".
tap press 6000
hold press 1500 6000
mark begin
# Home: next page has no book to turn; an unknown name is ignored.
vcmd PAGE_NEXT
wait 3000
vcmd FLY_TO_MOON
wait 1500
# Time (the RTC may not be set yet: then it says "no_clock"); battery 80 %.
vcmd TELL_TIME
wait 3000
battery 80 0
wait 4000
vcmd TELL_BATTERY
wait 3000
# Tell a story: the reader (or its no-book picture) opens; a status question
# over it is "busy"; next page turns the page or says there is no book.
vcmd OPEN_READER
wait 7000
vcmd TELL_BATTERY
wait 1500
vcmd PAGE_NEXT
wait 4000
# Home again.
hold press 1500 7000
battery off
# Bedtime: a safety alarm, then the sleep flow and a key press to cancel it.
alarm 30
vcmd SLEEP_REQUEST
wait 1500
tap press 6000
end
